pper .without-image"><div class="question-text text-ds-black-500">2. &nbsp; Which of the following metrics is most useful when the classes are imbalanced?</div></div></div><div class="options-container"><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">Accuracy</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">F1-Score</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">Recall</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">Specificity</span></div></div></button><button type="button" class="question-container btn-focus rounded-xl bg-white" data-cy="question-review-no-1" style="border-left-color: rgb(0, 201, 133);"><!----><div class="question-info-container"><!----><div class="question-text-wrapper .without-image"><div class="question-text text-ds-black-500">1. &nbsp; In rule-based induction, what happens when the rules are too specific to the training data? (CO3)</div></div></div><div class="options-container"><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">The model may suffer from overfitting.</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">The model will generalize better.</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">The rules will be shorter and more efficient.</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">The accuracy will always increase.</span></div></div></button><button type="button" c