/div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">Using more training samples</span></div></div></button><button type="button" class="question-container btn-focus rounded-xl bg-white" data-cy="question-review-no-5" style="border-left-color: rgb(0, 201, 133);"><!----><div class="question-info-container"><!----><div class="question-text-wrapper .without-image"><div class="question-text text-ds-black-500">5. &nbsp; Which of the following is an example of a rule-based induction algorithm?</div></div></div><div class="options-container"><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">Decision Tree</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">NaÃ¯ve Bayes</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">Support Vector Machine</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">K-Nearest Neighbors</span></div></div></button><button type="button" class="question-container btn-focus rounded-xl bg-white" data-cy="question-review-no-6" style="border-left-color: rgb(0, 201, 133);"><!----><div class="question-info-container"><!----><div class="question-text-wrapper .without-image"><div class="question-text text-ds-black-500">6. &nbsp; Bayesâ€™ Theorem is most useful when dealing with which type of probability?</div></div></div><div class="options-container"><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">Independent events</span></div><div class="option-container full-width"><!----><!----><div class="bullet"></div><span class="option-text text-ds-black-500">Conditional probability</span></